to DVS and DSA. Both DVS and DSA have fewer consulting staff than consulting students. The students offer a wider variety of disciplinary
backgrounds, far beyond what would be possible to hire and support if using only full-time staff. Consultants enable the department to take on a
high volume of support requests for short-term assistance, as well as work on longer-term projects with graduate students and faculty with the
DSA. The advantages of our service—our wide range of skill, timeliness and level of expertise—are entirely due to this combination of effort from
full-time librarians and our student consultant staff.
4 | NC STATE'S SERVICE MODEL
The Data Science Consulting Service at NC State University is driven by DVS and DSA. The Libraries launched DVS in 2018 in response to a need
for basic services to support data analysis and statistical programming. In addition to data science consulting, DVS offers course-integrated
instruction, open workshops on data science topics and specialised computer lab spaces at NC State. We currently offer data science instruction
in workshop and course-integrated sessions format in the areas of visualisation design, Python and R programming and GIS.
DSA was launched in 2021 with a similar mission to make data science support more accessible. DSA brings data science support across the
entire NC State University community, outside of a particular department or college, through all three pillars of the land grant mission: education,
research and service to the state of North Carolina. The DSA does this through teaching, research enablement and consulting. DSA operates
under the principle that ‘data science is for everyone’, whereas the Libraries' vision statement is ‘NC State's competitive edge'. Together, DVS
and the DSA offer a data science consulting program that is free and open to everyone affiliated with NC State University and at any stage of
their project or research. We believe that by existing in the spaces that the campus already utilises (i.e. the Libraries), we can better engage the
community and offer support services that they may need but not know are available to them.
The NC State community has demonstrated a growing need for data services, and DVS provides spaces within the Libraries to support data
science research through consulting. Through the Data Science Consulting Service in DVS, NC State University Libraries' solution to address
research support needs has been to cultivate a team of graduate student employees from diverse disciplines to offer consultations on data science
(e.g. programming, statistics and visualisation) problems. Our model is designed around short consultation sessions led by our DSCs, with high
performance computing data science lab spaces in the Hill Library and the Hunt Library. In the last 5 years, these Data Science Consultants served
