4.2 | Consultant staffing
DVS employs graduate students from different disciplines based on the current and projected needs of the program and the students' qualifica
tions. The hiring process is led by full-time librarian faculty with relevant technical expertise, as well as a support staff member who supervises
the students and handles scheduling and communication.
The librarians supervise consultants with similar technical expertise, help them deal with challenging consultations and mentor them to
develop their professional skills. The graduate students bring experience and knowledge of diverse fields to our service, which helps build a
technically rich environment to cover many distinct issues faced by university researchers.
Hiring graduate students as our consultants is the key to the success and sustainability of our consultation services. We hire mostly for hourly
positions, with a limited number of Graduate Research Assistantships (GRAs) available. Our services offer the students an on-campus position that
provides valuable work experience in their field. This opportunity helps students who require funding to continue their education and contributes
to the stated student success goals of NC State University Libraries (NC State University Libraries, 2022).
4.2.1 | Hiring considerations
Our hiring process is geared towards representing a broad range of disciplines, as well as robust support for our core software tools. Desirable
candidates have both a strong technical background for data science consulting and the aptitude for effective consulting as shown by their intel
lectual curiosity and interest in helping others learn. Data science consulting is inherently collaborative, and successful candidates demonstrate
the ability to learn new techniques and domain knowledge, a commitment to helping others and a genuine enjoyment of this process. Over the
past several years, our department has employed graduate students pursuing degrees in geospatial analytics, psychology, statistics, textiles,
