APPENDIX A
Institutions scanned were selected from the following sources to ensure a variety of program types were represented among institutions that
have demonstrated a focus on data science or offer growing data support. ‘Academic Data Science Centers in the United States’ explores 2018
examples of new or growing data science programs, now more established. All schools listed in ‘Academic Data Science Centers in the
United States’ are represented in this scan as the study is a leading publication on diverse American data science education environments, though
the source is also not completely representative in and of itself. A subset of schools randomly selected from 2023 Alfred P. Sloan grant recipients
show a snapshot of recent innovators in STEM. Members of the ADSA were also randomly selected as they range in the size and reach of their
programs but nonetheless demonstrate a concerted interest in participating in the discourse and development of data science education. Several
smaller institutions were selected based on the recommendation of colleagues to in an effort to represent smaller universities that may have
fewer data science offerings or resources. Approximately half (n 1⁄4 25) of these institutions are present in more than one of the sources.
